  <way id="160016053" version="8" timestamp="2020-07-11T21:46:33Z" changeset="87864598" uid="11286310" user="Manateedriver">
    <nd ref="364789475"/>
    <nd ref="2626372447"/>
    <nd ref="2626372448"/>
    <nd ref="2626517532"/>
    <nd ref="2626372449"/>
    <nd ref="730709060"/>
    <nd ref="2626372450"/>
    <nd ref="1720805714"/>
    <nd ref="2626372451"/>
    <nd ref="2626517553"/>
    <tag k="highway" v="tertiary"/>
    <tag k="maxspeed" v="30 mph"/>
    <tag k="maxweight" v="7.5"/>
    <tag k="name" v="Captain's Hill"/>
    <tag k="note" v="OS Opendata Locator suggests this is also part of Kinwarton Road, but based on house numbers on the parallel road it should be Captain's Hill?"/>
    <tag k="note:2" v="This looks like it was built in a &quot;Gardencity&quot; arangement with a main road flanked with quite roads built to serve ribbion-development housing, caractorised also by the gardenscapes made between the roads in order to make live on the main road more"/>
    <tag k="note:3" v="pleasent. Often the paralel roads are named as the same or annoted with a west/east/south/north depending on witch side of the main the service road ran. Other places give different names. In this example both approches have been used depending by"/>
    <tag k="note:4" v="coincdence on which side of the parish boundry it was? The council adopted a road number of C205 for Kinwarton Road which sugests that Kinwarton Rd is thought by some to run up to the junction with B-road attibuted to Captain's Hill. the minor vertion"/>
    <tag k="note:5" v="Captain's Hill still needs to to the next junction so it goes on to the jcn with Throckmorton Road and turns into Ten Acres. Given the changes and maybe once another imaginary sevice road on the north side of the main road;the houses were numbered as if"/>
    <tag k="note:6" v="still runing by Captain's Hill. Estates being built in phases may have encoraged the mismatch with chges to the roads being made after one phase had already been establised on the edge of open land? This is based on probable speculation but seems logical"/>
    <tag k="note:7" v="till someone researches the truth."/>
    <tag k="source" v="npe"/>
    <tag k="surface" v="asphalt"/>
  </way>
